  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 140 PM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nThe active pattern continues Monday through Wednesday night, as \nupper ridging begins to amplify across the western CONUS. This leads \nto a west-northwest flow aloft. Guidance suggests occasional \ndisturbances will progress through the mean flow aloft, with a \ndaily threat for showers and thunderstorms across the area. PWAT\nvalues will also fall into next week, as we lose the monsoonal \nmoisture with the transition to northwest flow. Some threat for \nsevere storms will also persist Monday, and also on Tuesday as a\ncold front drops through the region. The threat for thunderstorms\ncontinues through Wednesday night, with drier conditions expected\nThursday through Saturday as an upper ridge builds back over \nthe region. \n\nTemperatures look to remain near average Monday in the mid to up \n80s, to below average by Wednesday. This will keep any heat concerns \naway, with a pleasant week expected.",
